// vOSlab system index
// System invariant documentation only (no plans, no mutable docs)

## Structure

```
system/
├── boot/              ← system boot files
│   ├── boot_manifest.vsm
│   ├── communication_protocol.vsm
│   ├── core_boot_primer.vsm
│   ├── covenant.vsm
│   ├── hard_rules.vsm
│   ├── regulation_layer.vsm
│   └── vsl_language_primer.vsm
├── kernel/            ← theoretical core of the system
│   ├── kernel-map-v1/
│   ├── theory-01/
│   ├── theory-02/
│   └── theory-lr-01/
├── instance/          ← instance configuration
│   ├── infra/
│   ├── inst-validation-01/
│   └── vsf-instance-v1/
├── rules/             ← system rules
│   └── R_DOC.vsm
├── s1-operations/     ← operations (S1)
├── s2-coordination/   ← coordination (S2)
├── s3-control/        ← control (S3)
├── s3star-audit/      ← audit (S3*)
├── s4-intelligence/   ← intelligence (S4)
└── s5-policy/         ← policy (S5)
```

## VSM components

### S1 - Operations
- `system/s1-operations/` — system tools and operations

### S2 - Coordination
- `system/s2-coordination/` — coordination between components

### S3 - Control
- `system/s3-control/` — control and monitoring

### S3* - Audit
- `system/s3star-audit/` — independent audit

### S4 - Intelligence
- `system/s4-intelligence/` — analysis and prediction

### S5 - Policy
- `system/s5-policy/` — high-level policies and rules

## Boot Files
- `system/boot/covenant.vsm` — constitutional covenant
- `system/boot/hard_rules.vsm` — hard rules (inviolable)
- `system/boot/core_boot_primer.vsm` — boot primitives

## Usage

To find system documentation:
1. Consult this index
2. Navigate by subsystem (S1-S5)
3. Read the corresponding file

NOTE: immutable documentation only. Plans go to `docs/plans/`.

